 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.6.2] — 2026-09-02 — Vercel Build Compatibility
+
+- Replaced private `vite/bin/vite.js` resolution with Vite's supported JavaScript `build()` API.
+- Migrated Overture vector-tile parsing to pbf v5 `PbfReader`.
+- Aligned React and React DOM at 19.2.8.
+- Pinned critical build/runtime packages to prevent Vercel cache/version drift.
+- Matched `puppeteer-core` 25.1.0 to Chromium 149.0.7827.22 used by `@sparticuz/chromium` 149.0.0.
+- Added dependency-API validation to the Vercel prebuild gate.
+- Added npm install-script approvals for the reviewed Sharp and esbuild versions.
+
+## [0.6.1] — 2026-09-02 — Free Commercial Intelligence
+
+### Added
+
+- Added a Next.js 16 server/API layer while preserving the original God’s Eye View Vite client as the top-level product surface.
+- Added native Commercial Recon, Commercial Markets, and Commercial Businesses layers using the original mission launcher, command dock, layer registry, camera and world-overlay systems.
+- Added zero-key business discovery through Overture Maps Places PMTiles, with optional Geoapify acceleration.
+- Added deterministic website audits, commercial-strength scoring, contactability, independence confidence, and Rebuild Opportunity scoring.
+- Added optional Gemini visual analysis with deterministic fallback when Gemini is not configured.
+- Added self-hosted Vercel Chromium capture using `puppeteer-core`, `@sparticuz/chromium-min`, and a build-time deployment-hosted Chromium pack. Browserless is not required.
+- Added country-level Market Recon with drill-down into business discovery.
+- Added Next.js counterparts for every same-origin `/api/*` proxy family shipped by the original Vite server.
+- Added free provider health, saved targets, recent commercial operations, QUICK/STANDARD/DEEP research modes and target cycling.
+- Added release validation and co